 at index `i` of the slice, counted from the start of the slice, in the\nunderlying array. The array is updated in place when neither it nor the slice is shared, so a slice\ntaken from an array that is no longer used writes into that array. `s.array` gives back the whole\narray afterwards.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/UInt32/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.UInt32Array.Slice.set","kind":"def","line":36,"name":"ScalarArray.UInt32Array.Slice.set","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/UInt32/InPlace.lean#L36-L48"}}],"imports":["Init","Init.Data.Iterators.Lemmas.Basic","Init.Data.Slice.InternalLemmas","ScalarArray.Internal","ScalarArray.UInt32.Array","ScalarArray.UInt32.Basic","ScalarArray.UInt32.Lemmas","ScalarArray.UInt32.Program","ScalarArray.UInt32.Slice"],"instances":[],"name":"ScalarArray.UInt32.InPlace"}